# Remove Hardcoded Values & Implement Database-Driven Dynamic Data for Terminal

Remove all hardcoded and mock values from the trading terminal (`/admin/terminal` and `/terminal`, rendered via `frontend/src/pages/Trade.tsx`) and underlying backend endpoints. Ensure all data is queried from the database/broker adapter with robust fallbacks (`blank`, `"-"`, `0`) and comprehensive error handling so the page never breaks.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> - **Removal of Fake Synthetic Data**: Previously, if history, option chain, or depth data was missing, the UI fabricated fake candlestick bars (`generateSyntheticBars`), fake option chain strikes/OI/IV (`generateOptionChain`), and fake depth bids/asks (`generateMarketDepth`). These will be replaced with real database/broker queries. When data is absent from the database, the UI will cleanly display `-`, `0`, or an empty state instead of fabricated stock data.
> - **Index Ticker Bar**: Initial hardcoded mock prices (`23724.67`, `51200.00`, etc.) will be removed. The ticker will start in a clean pending state (`—` / `-`) and populate dynamically from DB/broker quotes and WebSocket ticks.
> - **API Keys**: Hardcoded Kite API keys (`"ouuv4g2r3iyafu5c"`, `"jfwd2gvwal8pq0rp"`) are completely removed from the frontend. Auth URLs are dynamically obtained from the backend.

